<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="70780" href="schedule/2021/fall/BIOE/598/70780.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2021" href="schedule/2021.xml">2021</calendarYear><term id="120218" href="schedule/2021/fall.xml">Fall 2021</term><subject id="BIOE" href="schedule/2021/fall/BIOE.xml">Bioengineering</subject><course id="598" href="schedule/2021/fall/BIOE/598.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>RD </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Single-Cell Decision-Making</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>An introduction to quantitative single molecule and single cell studies, including their role in disease, development, and decision-making processes. Decision making in viruses, prokaryotes, and eukaryotes will be discussed. The course will end with signaling in spatial patterning and morphogen gradients.This course offers opportunities for student-led seminar presentations, discussions of the scientific literature, and final group project presentations.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2021-08-23Z</startDate><endDate>2021-12-08Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="L2 ">Lecture</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>03:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2101</roomNumber><buildingName>Everitt Laboratory</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Dar" firstName="R">Dar, R</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>